WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.501
-Ah. That's what
I'm talking about.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.136
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:05.872
-Hey, how you doing?
-You know me.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.006
Come on.
-It's the big guy.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:10.409
-It's the big guy.
-The big guy.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:12.611
-The big guy.
Hey, you know what?

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:15.414
We were just talking to our
writers backstage.

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:17.150
Have you guys ever seen
a ghost before?

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.653
Have you ever been haunted?

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.221
-Mm, no.

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:24.390
-Tim says no. Swizz?

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.925
-I've definitely seen ghosts,

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.460
but I know them
every time I've seen them.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.228
You know when you see a ghost
you're like,

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:31.231
"That didn't happen"?

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.766
-You do that...
-But you know what you've seen.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.734
-...or do you acknowledge them
and make friends with them?

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.869
Like, that's what I do.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:40.406
-I mean, in one of my first
houses, I started to become,

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:41.841
you know,
friends with my ghost

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.542
and I'm like, "Just leave me
alone right now."

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:45.211
-Yeah. You go,
"I'm cool, right? It's me.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.446
I was just checking it out.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.714
You do whatever
you're going to do.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.415
You're a ghost
and that's cool, like --"

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:50.883
-Yeah. You're the big guy.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.385
They can't be around
the big guy.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.652
-You can't be around --
the big guy's here.

00:00:53.652 --> 00:00:56.756
The big guy is in my room.
I'm in my man cave.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:59.158
Doing big guy stuff.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:02.929
I think I've heard just so many
stories from you,

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.297
from Justin Timberlake, Tim...
-Yeah.

00:01:05.297 --> 00:01:07.667
-...and just how you guys just
like get along, you know,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.435
and I'm a little jealous,
but it's okay.

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:11.504
[ Laughter ]
I still got my --

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:14.406
I still got --
I got ghost friends.

00:01:14.406 --> 00:01:16.208
[ Laughter ]
-There he --

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:17.376
And he's there --

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:18.877
-Jimmy's still bringing
sexy back.

00:01:18.877 --> 00:01:19.945
Don't worry about it.

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:21.513
-Yeah, Jimmy.
You still got sexy back.

00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:23.048
-Thank you.
I appreciate that.

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:25.418
But what was the big --
do you remember

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.052
one of your first big things
where you were like,

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:30.289
"Oh, I did this. This is good."
Was it Missy? Was it --

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:34.260
-It was my first record

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.129
that was a hit...

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:39.231
actually was
an Aaliyah record,

00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:41.500
"If Your Girl Only Knew."

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.136
That was my first hit.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.871
-Wow.
-Then "Pony" was already out,

00:01:45.871 --> 00:01:48.073
and then "Pony" came
right after that.

00:01:48.073 --> 00:01:49.775
-Ginuwine.
That became --

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:52.378
-That was already out and it
was already bubbling,

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:55.447
but then after
"If Your Girl Only Knew,"

00:01:55.447 --> 00:01:58.884
and then that's when we all kind
of connected as a crew.

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:01.420
And then "Pony" started to rise,
and everybody was like,

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.088
what is this...
[ Imitates beat ]

00:02:03.088 --> 00:02:05.658
But it was taking over
the world. Nobody knew.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.693
And the video was out
and everything.

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:09.996
And then it just blew up
after that.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.131
-Swizz, what was --
your first one was --

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.333
Was it "Rough Ryders' Anthem?"
Was that DMX?

00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:16.603
-That dropped Yes.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.404
And that was a serious one.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:21.240
You know, growing up
in the Bronx

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.043
and sitting in the streets
of Harlem

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.878
while that record dropped,

00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:28.648
and...125th Street,

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:32.819
and to see every single car
drive past playing that song.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.921
But I'm sitting
on the fire hydrant

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.022
and nobody know that I produced
that song.

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:39.925
And just to see
the natural energy

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:42.361
of your surroundings

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:44.697
from something that
you produced in your room.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.266
DMX didn't want to do the song.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:49.501
He lost a bet with my uncle
playing cards

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:51.437
and he had to do the vocals
to "Stop, drop."

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.706
And at first I thought
he lost the bet,

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.842
but "Stop, drop" became so big,
I realized that he won the bet.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.377
So...
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:58.377 --> 00:02:59.711
Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:02:59.711 --> 00:03:01.748
So you guys get together.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:04.717
How did you decide to do
"Verzuz" during quarantine?

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.385
How did that all happen?

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:08.154
-You know,
Tim is a big instigator.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.590
You know, he's an instigator.
He likes to start fights

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.091
and, you know --
-That's true.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.525
-A real bully around these
places, you know.

00:03:13.525 --> 00:03:15.194
-Oh, my goodness.
Wow.

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.663
-That's how I kind of --
he's right.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:19.665
It started that way.
-Really?

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:21.601
-You know, the first,

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.836
I say the first time
everybody locked down,

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.871
we tripping out like,
what are we going to do?

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:29.308
We were just talking and talking
about life, and I just got into,

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:31.510
like, antagonizing mode.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:34.747
And I just started, like,
putting up video posts.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.882
And then he's like,
"I see what you're doing."

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:39.885
-No, no, no. You were saying,
"What you going to do, Swizz?

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:42.321
What are we doing, Swizz?"
-Really?

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:44.023
-"What are you thinking, Swizz?"
-And you go, let's do it.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.658
Let's go for it.
Let's see who has --

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.426
Let's go for it.
Prove it to everybody.

00:03:47.426 --> 00:03:49.228
Let's go on Instagram Live.
-Yes.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:52.064
-At first it was more of a,
really was a kind of

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:54.767
a competition, but then
I think it kind of grew

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:58.370
into kind of more
of a mutual admiration.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:01.640
And, like, fans kind of,
and stans going at each other

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.576
like, "Oh, you can't even
touch Babyface --"

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.545
That was it --
Babyface, by the way.

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.046
That was the one.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.381
-Babyface and Teddy Riley?

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:11.150
-That broke the Internet.
That broke everything.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.619
I go like, "Babyface,
what's going on?

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.153
Like, I got to check this out."

00:04:15.153 --> 00:04:16.555
This is such a good idea,

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.357
because
it's friendly competition.

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:19.524
But I go like --
I forgot how many --

00:04:19.524 --> 00:04:20.893
-Educational celebration.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.463
-Yeah, I forgot how many
good jams he had.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.832
-Whew. Me too.
-Yes. Whew.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:28.934
And now there's something called
the "Verzuz Effect."

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:30.069
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.871
-Can you explain what
that is?

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:36.609
-It's a multitude of things.
It's record sales, streaming,

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:39.945
you know, because we're in
the world of streaming,

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:42.348
and now you have catalogs,

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:45.218
we're moving the streams
of catalogs going up.

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:48.354
People are getting
work requests.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.855
Everything is happening.

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:52.525
And every day like we might --
me and Swizz will get

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.627
something that happened from
"Verzuz," and we're like,

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.562
"Ooh, the 'Verzuz Effect.'"

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.163
-It is.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:04:59.999
-Like the album being --

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.101
I think Brandy's
album was at 40

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.969
and it went to number 1.
-Yep.

00:05:03.969 --> 00:05:06.372
-That was a great one too.
Brandy. Oh, my God.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.806
-Brandy and Monica.
-And Monica.

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:09.074
It was unbelievable.

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:11.744
I love Gladys Knight
and Patty La Belle.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.178
-Ooh!
-Ooh!

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:14.713
-Did you see the commercials
for that?

00:05:14.713 --> 00:05:16.416
-No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:18.016
I can't even --
and I can't pick --

00:05:18.016 --> 00:05:21.521
-I wanted to bite my phone.
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:25.224
-I know season two of
"Verzuz" is coming soon,

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.426
and I know you can't tell us
who's going to be on it,

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:30.563
but come on.
It's the big man.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.631
-It's the big guy.
-It's the big guy.

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:33.833
-The big guy.

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.768
-You can't tell big guy
what's going on?

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.069
-Go ahead, give him
a little something.

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:39.571
-I got a phone call from
a friend named Busta Rhymes,

00:05:39.571 --> 00:05:43.976
who says that he's ready

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.945
for any type of "Verzuz" action

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:48.614
out there
that's coming his way.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.449
-What?
-So Busta Rhymes...

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:52.318
-Oh, no, no.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:54.720
-"Put Your Hands Where
My Eyes Could See."

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.057
-Oh, my gosh.
-Janet Jackson, Busta Rhymes.

00:05:58.057 --> 00:06:00.026
-Dude if Bust--
So Busta --

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:02.561
Who's gonna --
who will accept?

00:06:02.561 --> 00:06:03.863
Who will accept and go up
against --

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:05.130
-That's the question
that we have for you.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.400
Will you accept?
-Yeah.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.869
I'm ready to go head to head
against --

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:12.171
-The big guy.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:13.505
-I don't even want to --

00:06:13.505 --> 00:06:15.507
I don't want to put my hands
where his eyes can see.

00:06:15.507 --> 00:06:17.109
I'll just let him -- No.
He would destroy --

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:18.311
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:20.112
Can you imagine?

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:23.549
You should do that "Verzuz."
A comedy "Verzuz."

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:26.919
Two dudes that can't rap
go at it.

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:28.654
I'll be on that one
if you want to do --

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:30.455
I would watch that any second,
Busta Rhymes.

00:06:30.455 --> 00:06:32.224
I love him too.

00:06:32.224 --> 00:06:33.893
Who's it going to be?
That's going to be exciting.

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:37.730
-But season two is going to be
big levels.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.065
Big, big levels.

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:42.367
A lot of people that weren't
ready are ready now.

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:44.870
Because, you know, when we ask
people to do "Verzuz,"

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:46.872
the first thing they say is no.
-Yep.

00:06:46.872 --> 00:06:49.141
-Yes.
-A hundred percent.

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:51.443
The first thing they say is,
"No. That's not my thing.

00:06:51.443 --> 00:06:52.712
I like to watch that.

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:54.246
I don't really want to be
a part of it."

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:56.482
But then, you know --
because it takes time.

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:58.951
They have to go set up
with a DJ.

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:02.054
They have to revisit their
catalog themselves.

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:04.590
They have to get the confidence
where they need to be.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.125
And they have to really
start to understand

00:07:07.125 --> 00:07:10.296
how it can be beneficial
and successful for them.

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:11.930
And for me I'm like, listen,

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.899
no matter what you do
it's a plus.

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:16.268
The only thing you can have
a problem if you don't use

00:07:16.268 --> 00:07:19.805
our tech team, which we have
built in.

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:21.607
And that's the problem
that Teddy Riley had.

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:23.642
Everybody wants to use
their own tech team

00:07:23.642 --> 00:07:26.245
and be mad scientists.
It doesn't work.

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:28.748
So, if you listen
to the guidelines

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.616
and the "Verzuz" tech team
is used --

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:32.385
-It works.
-Scientists.

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:33.986
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:35.521
-Listen to the scientists!

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.456
I've been saying this
the whole time!

00:07:37.456 --> 00:07:39.625
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.526
-I've been saying it
the whole time,

00:07:41.526 --> 00:07:44.930
listen to the scientists,
please.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.598
Congrats on that
and hank you so much.

00:07:46.598 --> 00:07:48.434
It's a gift that
keeps on giving.

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:50.236
Swizz Beatz, Timbaland.

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:52.271
Season two of "Verzuz"
is coming soon

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:54.407
to Instagram TV and Apple Music.

